[00:07.14]Hello. Can I help you?
[00:10.24]Yes, I’d like a cheese and tomato roll, please.
[00:14.70]Do you want the roll hot?
[00:17.72]Yes, please.
[00:18.84]Would you like something to drink?
[00:21.44]Yes, I’d like an apple juice, please.
[00:25.22]So that’s a roll and an apple juice. Is that all?
[00:32.14]Er, I’d like some carrot cake, too.
[00:36.22]OK, that’s £8 altogether.
[00:40.74]Here you are.
[00:41.90]And that’s £2 change. The roll will be a few minutes. We’ll bring it to your table.
[00:49.86]Thank you.
[00:51.02]Enjoy your meal. And what can I get for you?
[00:55.48]I’d like the chicken and mushroom soup, please, and an apple juice.
[01:00.16]OK. Anything else?
[01:03.16]No, I think that’s all.
[01:04.82]What! No cake? But you said …
[01:08.90]I’m trying to be good. I only buy cake at the weekends.
[01:12.98]Really?
[01:14.66]Yes, I’m being careful with what I eat. Have you got a problem with that?
[01:19.58]No, not at all.
[01:22.90]OK, that’s £6.50.
[01:25.30]Can I pay by card?
[01:27.66]Of course. Just put it in here.
[01:31.40]It’s done.
[01:32.20]Thanks. We’ll bring the soup over in a minute or two.
[01:36.16]Could you bring me a fork with it, too?
[01:39.16]Sure.
[01:39.60]A fork? What do you need a fork for? You can’t eat soup with a fork.
[01:45.86]I’ve got my reasons. Don’t you worry about it.
[01:51.20]Moments later …
[01:55.12]Well, you’re right. This is a good roll. How’s the soup?
[02:01.84]Delicious. Would you like to try some?
[02:04.86]No, I’m OK. My cake looks fantastic, doesn’t it?
[02:10.48]Yes, it does. Mmmmm … it tastes fantastic, too!
[02:15.28]Hey, what are you doing?
[02:18.60]Mmmmm. That is a good cake!
[02:21.42]But you said, cake only at the weekends.
[02:25.06]I said I only buy cake at the weekends.
[02:29.62]And?
[02:30.76]Well, you bought this cake. I’ve got no problem eating your cake.
[02:36.26]And that explains the fork.
[02:38.88]Yes, it does. Now hurry up and finish your roll before I eat all your cake.
